532: ### CVE-2025-29927 â€” Middleware Authorization Bypass (CVSS 9.1, Critical)
534: An attacker can bypass middleware-based authorization by sending a crafted `x-middleware-subrequest` header, skipping all middleware logic. This affects any Next.js application that relies on `middleware.ts` (or `proxy.ts` in 16+) as the **sole** authorization gate. Patched in Next.js 14.2.25, 15.2.3, and all 16.x releases.
